//! The OpenAPI 3.1 document, generated by utoipa from the handlers.
//!
//! It is committed as `openapi/stepclimb.json`; `just openapi-diff` regenerates it and the
//! TypeScript client (`packages/api-client`) and fails when either differs from what is
//! committed. Today it lists the operations probes, which the web app's skeleton route calls
//! through the generated client, sign-out, `GET /api/v1/me` and the user's appearance choice, the caller's organization, its
//! settings and its entitlements, the account tree, the permission catalog, roles and role
//! assignment routes under `/api/v1/admin`, the user admin routes, users' identities and the
//! signed-in user's, the organization's branding and its stylesheet (`/theme.css`), the web app
//! manifest (`/manifest.webmanifest`), the local
//! sign-in switches, enrollment links, the enrollment start route, passkey registration
//! through a link and passkey sign-in, the start of sign-in with an outside identity provider,
//! the signed-in user's passkeys, password enrollment, sign-in and change, TOTP enrollment,
//! its sign-in step and disabling, the discovery document (`/.well-known/stepclimb`), the OAuth
//! 2.1 authorization, token and revocation endpoints for Stepclimb's own apps (`/oauth/authorize`,
//! `/oauth/token`, `/oauth/revoke`), service
//! accounts and their API keys, course file uploads and the files area, a course's pages and
//! their versions, video uploads (tus) and the videos of a course, a learner's progress steps,
//! the staff progress reads and the progress event bodies, the completion history, and the shared error
//! schemas and responses below. The other M0 specs add their endpoints under `/api/v1`.
//!
//! Every `/api/v1` operation lists its errors in `#[utoipa::path]` (spec 02 B6). The errors
//! common to every operation reference the responses here, such as
//! `(status = 400, response = BadRequest)`, so each error body is documented once.

